ref_dict.thm: quantitative Pansu:
\begin{thm}\label{thm: quantitative Pansu}
 Let $G$ be a simply connected nilpotent sub-Finsler Lie group. With respect to an asymptotic grading, consider the Pansu limit metric $\rho_0$ on $G$ and the contracted metrics $\rho_\epsilon$. Then, for every compact set $K \subseteq G$, there is a constant $C>0$ such that
 \begin{equation}\label{eq: thm: quantitative pansu}
  \left|\rho_0(p,q)-\rho_\epsilon(p,q)\right| \leq C \epsilon^{\alpha_{\infty}/\beta}, \quad \forall \epsilon \in [0,1], \; \forall p,q \in K,
 \end{equation}
  where $\alpha_{\infty}$ and $\beta$ are the constants from Definition~\ref{def: constant alpha pansu} and~\ref{def: constant beta}.
\end{thm}

ref_dict.main thm: pansu:
\begin{thm}[Quantitative Pansu]\label{main thm: pansu}
 Let $(G,d)$ be a geodesic Lie group. Assume $G$ is simply connected and nilpotent.
 After fixing an asymptotic grading, consider the associated Pansu limit metric $d_\infty$ on $G$ and the constants $\alpha_\infty$ and $\beta$ defined in \eqref{def_alpha_inf} and \eqref{def_beta}, respectively. Then, for some $C>0$, we have 
 \begin{align}\label{eq: main pansu1}
  \left|d(p,q)-d_\infty(p,q)\right| \leq C\max\left\{d_\infty(1,p),d_\infty(1,q)\right\}^{1-\alpha_\infty/\beta}, \quad \forall p\in G, \;\forall q \in G \setminus B_{d_\infty}(1,1).
 \end{align}
\end{thm}

expanded_sketch:
We briefly summarize the strategy to obtain the theorems, focusing on Theorem~\ref{main thm: pansu}. One considers a one-parameter family of Lie group products $(*_\epsilon)_{\epsilon\in \mathbb{R}}$ on $G$ with $G=(G,*_1)$ and $(G,*_0)$ isomorphic to the asymptotic cone of $G$. Then one introduces a one-parameter family of geodesic metrics $(\rho_\epsilon)_{\epsilon\in \mathbb{R}}$ such that $\rho_\epsilon$ is $*_\epsilon$-left-invariant, $\rho_1=d$, and $\rho_0=d_\infty$.

To prove the main theorem, we deduce it from the following auxiliary result.

\begin{thm}\label{thm: quantitative Pansu}
 Let $G$ be a simply connected nilpotent sub-Finsler Lie group. With respect to an asymptotic grading, consider the Pansu limit metric $\rho_0$ on $G$ and the contracted metrics $\rho_\epsilon$. Then, for every compact set $K \subseteq G$, there is a constant $C>0$ such that
 \begin{equation}\label{eq: thm: quantitative pansu}
  \left|\rho_0(p,q)-\rho_\epsilon(p,q)\right| \leq C \epsilon^{\alpha_{\infty}/\beta}, \quad \forall \epsilon \in [0,1], \; \forall p,q \in K,
 \end{equation}
  where $\alpha_{\infty}$ and $\beta$ are the constants from Definition~\ref{def: constant alpha pansu} and~\ref{def: constant beta}.
\end{thm}

In particular, this gives uniform quantitative convergence on compacts: for every compact $K\subseteq G$ there exists $C$ such that
\begin{equation}\label{eq: thm: quantitative pansu}
  \left|\rho_0(p,q)-\rho_\epsilon(p,q)\right| \leq C \epsilon^{\alpha_{\infty}/\beta}, \quad \forall \epsilon \in [0,1], \; \forall p,q \in K,
\end{equation}
To prove (say) $\rho_0(p,q)-\rho_\epsilon(p,q)\lesssim \epsilon^{\alpha_{\infty}/\beta}$ on a fixed compact $K$, one starts with a $\rho_\epsilon$-geodesic $\gamma$ from $p$ to $q$, constructs a curve $\gamma_0$ with $\gamma_0(0)=p$ and $\mathrm{Length}_{\rho_0}(\gamma_0)\le \mathrm{Length}_{\rho_\epsilon}(\gamma)$, and then bounds the $\rho_0$-distance between the endpoints of $\gamma$ and $\gamma_0$.

For the endpoint control, one observes that for every Carnot quotient ideal $\mathfrak{i}\triangleleft \mathrm{Lie}(G)$ and every $\epsilon\in[0,1]$, the curve $t\mapsto \gamma_\epsilon^{-1}(t)*_\epsilon\gamma(t)$ lies in $\mathfrak{i}$. Using the Ball-Box Theorem and the definition of $\beta$, together with a Grönwall-type lemma and the definition of $\alpha_\infty$, one bounds the $\rho_0$-distance of the endpoints of $\gamma$ and $\gamma_0$. The reverse inequality is proved with the same techniques.

