theorem.content:
\label{main_thm} Let $\mathcal{P}_N$ be the regular $N$-polygon of area $\pi$ with $N \geq 3$ sides. Then
    \begin{equation*}
        \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_3) > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_4) > \dots > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_N) > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_{N+1}) > \dots > \lambda_1(\mathbb{D}) \, ,
    \end{equation*}
    where $\mathbb{D}$ is the unit disk. That is, the first Dirichlet eigenvalues are monotonically decreasing in $N$.

    Furthermore, let $q_N = \frac{\lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_N)}{\lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_{N+1})}$. Then it also holds
    \begin{equation*}
       q_3 > q_4 > \dots > q_N > q_{N+1} > \dots > 1 \, .
    \end{equation*}

