[Quantitative supercritical disconnection bound]\label{thm:main-intro}
Let $G=(V,E)$ be an infinite, connected, locally finite graph, let $p>p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$,
and let $S\subset V$ be any (finite or infinite) set of vertices.
Then
\begin{equation}\label{eq:main}
\mathbb{P}_{p}(S\nleftrightarrow\infty)
\le
\inf_{\substack{p_{1}\in(p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G),\,p)\\ \varepsilon,\delta\in(0,1)}}
\left[
\frac{\delta\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
{1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
\;+\;
(1+\delta)\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)\,
\mathrm{PK}_{p,\delta,\,1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)}}(S)}
\right].
\end{equation}

sketch:
The proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main-intro} is described as an “FCA mechanism” with three ingredients:
\begin{itemize}
\item a \emph{functional input}: use the local functional $\phi^{p}_{v}(S)$ from \cite{ZL24}, which “characterizes $p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ through finite-volume connectivity data”;
\item a \emph{cutset/local-boundary step}: “for each chosen vertex, we compare disconnection from infinity with disconnection from an inner boundary of a ball (in an iteratively punctured graph)”;
\item an \emph{amplification step}: “by selecting well-separated vertices (the packing), we exploit independence to amplify a uniform positive probability of connection to infinity into an exponential bound for the joint disconnection event.”
\end{itemize}
More concretely, the characterization theorem of \cite{ZL24} implies that for $p>p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ “one can find vertices whose local functionals are uniformly close to $1$ for \emph{all} finite sets containing them as interior points”; this gives “a robust lower bound on the probability of connecting to infinity” and produces the “good” vertices used in the packing construction. The quantitative bound \eqref{eq:main} is then obtained “from an induction-on-packing argument,” together with the amplification lemmas.

expanded_sketch:
The proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:main-intro} is described as an “FCA mechanism” with three ingredients:
\begin{itemize}
\item a \emph{functional input}: use the local functional $\phi^{p}_{v}(S)$ from Zhen and Li, \emph{Characterizes $p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ through finite-volume connectivity data} (2024), which “characterizes $p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ through finite-volume connectivity data”;
\item a \emph{cutset/local-boundary step}: “for each chosen vertex, we compare disconnection from infinity with disconnection from an inner boundary of a ball (in an iteratively punctured graph)”;
\item an \emph{amplification step}: “by selecting well-separated vertices (the packing), we exploit independence to amplify a uniform positive probability of connection to infinity into an exponential bound for the joint disconnection event.”
\end{itemize}
More concretely, the characterization theorem of Zhen and Li, \emph{Characterizes $p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ through finite-volume connectivity data} (2024) implies that for $p>p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$ “one can find vertices whose local functionals are uniformly close to $1$ for \emph{all} finite sets containing them as interior points”; this gives “a robust lower bound on the probability of connecting to infinity” and produces the “good” vertices used in the packing construction. The quantitative bound
\begin{equation}\label{eq:main}
\mathbb{P}_{p}(S\nleftrightarrow\infty)
\le
\inf_{\substack{p_{1}\in(p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G),\,p)\\ \varepsilon,\delta\in(0,1)}}
\left[
\frac{\delta\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
{1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
\;+\;
(1+\delta)\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)\,
\mathrm{PK}_{p,\delta,\,1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)}}(S)}
\right].
\end{equation}
is then obtained “from an induction-on-packing argument,” together with the amplification lemmas.,

expanded_theorem:
[Quantitative supercritical disconnection bound]\label{thm:main-intro}
Let $G=(V,E)$ be an infinite, connected, locally finite graph, let $p>p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G)$,
and let $S\subset V$ be any (finite or infinite) set of vertices.
Then
\begin{equation}\label{eq:main}
\mathbb{P}_{p}(S\nleftrightarrow\infty)
\le
\inf_{\substack{p_{1}\in(p^{\mathrm{site}}_{c}(G),\,p)\\ \varepsilon,\delta\in(0,1)}}
\left[
\frac{\delta\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
{1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{1-\varepsilon}}
\;+\;
(1+\delta)\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)\,
\mathrm{PK}_{p,\delta,\,1-\left(\frac{1-p}{1-p_{1}}\right)^{(1-\varepsilon)}}(S)}
\right].
\end{equation}

